# Runtime model cache (YOLOE checkpoint, MobileCLIP text encoder, HF snapshots). Only
# appears with the bind-mount fallback; the named-volume path stores it under podman's
# graphroot. Ignored either way.
.cache
.hf_cache/
models/*
tags/*
test-output/*
# version/*
# output of the ungated calibration run (scripts/calibrate_class_conf.py)
calib-out/
# frozen evaluation frames (~75 MB) and their UI thumbnails. Regenerate deterministically
# with `python eval/freeze_frames.py`; eval/frames.json is the committed source of truth.
eval/frames/
eval/thumbs/
eval/*-out/
__pycache__
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
test-files/long/
smoke-in/
smoke-out/

# 2-minute NBA segment cut from test-files/long/ for the config A/B video check;
# regenerate with the ffmpeg line in eval/experiments/10_config_ab/README.md
test-files/seg/
# frame samples extracted from full titles by eval/box_gt/sample_frames.sh
test-files/frames/
test-files/val/
# ---- experiment run outputs -------------------------------------------------------
#
# The rule: a run whose vectors were STRIPPED is committed, a run that kept them is not.
# Stripped runs are ~50-600 KB each and are the evidence behind the scored tables, so
# 10_config_ab, 13_sliced and 14_yoloe_imgsz are all in the repo. A 768-float array per tag
# is ~97% of the file, which is the whole difference: 5 GB against 13 MB.
#
# There is no filename convention separating them, so each vector-carrying run needs its own
# line here. If you add an experiment that keeps vectors, add it below.

# title runs keep their vectors (retrieval question) and are ~1.4 GB
eval/experiments/11_titles/*/*/out.jsonl
# SigLIP-embedded reference pool, rebuildable with eval/box_gt/build_logo_pool.py
eval/experiments/12_logo_pool/*.npz
# temporal runs keep their vectors too -- the whole question is whether grouping loses recall,
# which cannot be asked without them. 5.0 GB across eight arms.
eval/experiments/15_temporal/*/*/out.jsonl
# the aggregator's index-shaped output: `keep` vectors per track, 2.2 GB. Regenerate with
# eval/tools/aggregate_temporal.py -- but note that needs the out.jsonl above, so regenerating
# from a clean checkout means re-running the tagger.
**/track_vectors.jsonl
#
# `appearances.jsonl` is deliberately NOT ignored despite being 20 MB. It carries no vectors,
# it is the coverage report itself rather than an intermediate, and once the two files above
# are gone it is the only surviving artifact of a run that costs hours of GPU to reproduce.

# container stdout from eval/box_gt/run_config_ab.sh, kept only while a run is being debugged
eval/experiments/*/*/*/run.log
